      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Unfortunately, this is impossible. While the devs could certainly raise the limits for how many polygons load in for Quest or whitelist more shaders/allow custom shaders, they cannot load unity content built for a different architecture. A fun side effect of this is that creators can actually make quest-only avatars that will appear as a robot on PC. Idk why people do it, but it still happens nonetheless. It's not a limitation made by VRChat, but the Unity engine it runs on.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
